  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing a two-hour set at Broadberry in Richmond, Virginia, on August 28, 2022 [1]. Taped by Brandon, the 117-minute file documents 23 songs, making it the only available recording of this specific show [1]. The lineup includes five tracks from the album Bleed Out, with “Extraction Point” receiving its earliest recording in the archive [1]. The band also drew material from thirteen other albums, creating a diverse retrospective [1]. A notable highlight is a three-song solo section featuring older material, which includes a track that is the earliest recording in the archive, arriving 25 years later than its studio release [1]. The setlist moves through tracks like “Make You Suffer” and “Woke Up New” before reaching the solo performances of “Feed This End” and “Island Garden Song” [1]. “I Will Grab You by the Ears” also makes its earliest archive appearance during this solo segment [1]. The performance continues with “Before I Got There” and “The Diaz Brothers” before “First Blood” and “Damn These Vampires” [1]. A banter and jam section precedes “No Children,” which features a five-minute introductory jam [1]. The set concludes with “The Mess Inside,” “Wage Wars Get Rich Die Handsome,” and “Training Montage” [1]. Garcia Peoples provided support for the evening [1]. This recording is recommended for its complete track listing and documented lineage [1].",
